.TH TENSPILE 1 "30 October 2026" "tenspile 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tenspile \- inspect and edit tensor containers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B tenspile \-c
[\fB\-f\fR] \fIarchive\fR [\fIkey=file\fR ...]
.B tenspile \-t
[\fB\-v\fR] [\fB\-\-columns\fR] [\fB\-\-fold\fR] [\fB\-f\fR] \fIarchive\fR [\fIkey\fR ...]
.B tenspile \-x
[\fB\-f\fR] \fIarchive\fR [\fIkey\fR ...]
.B tenspile \-r
[\fB\-f\fR] \fIarchive\fR \fIkey=file\fR ...
.B tenspile \-u
[\fB\-f\fR] \fIarchive\fR \fIkey=file\fR ...
.B tenspile \-\-delete
[\fB\-f\fR] \fIarchive\fR \fIkey\fR ...
.B tenspile \-i
[\fB\-f\fR] \fIarchive\fR
.B tenspile
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tenspile
creates, lists, extracts, and edits files that store tensors.
One invocation does one operation.
Short flags cluster, as in
.BR "tenspile \-tvf model.safetensors" .
A directory is the safetensors weight set inside it:
one
.I *.safetensors.index.json
if that is the only index, otherwise one loose
.I *.safetensors
file.
A lone
.I .safetensors
file beside
.I config.json
is refused unless
.B \-\-force\-single\-file
is written immediately before that path.
.PP
List and info read the header.
They do not load weight bytes.
A rewrite streams unchanged tensor bytes into the new file.
.PP
Comparison is
.BR tensdiff (1).
Renaming tensors into GGUF names is
.BR tensconv (1).
Dequantizing a pack is
.BR tensquant (1).
.SH OPTIONS
Exactly one operation is required.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-create
Create an archive.
Refuses to overwrite an existing file unless
.B \-\-force
is set.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-list
List member names.
.B \-v
adds dtype, shape, bytes, offset, and parameters.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extract
Extract members.
No names means all of them.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-append
Add members.
Errors if a tensor key already exists.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Replace a tensor key, or add it if it is missing.
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Remove tensor keys and write the archive again.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-info
Summarize the archive from its header:
format, version, member count, data bytes, metadata, a dtype tally,
and any notes.
On a directory, a sibling
.I config.json
with
.I quantization_config.quant_method
or an MLX
.I quantization
object adds one note of method, bits, and group size.
The weights stay packed.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIfile\fR"
Archive path.
If omitted, the first operand is the archive.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Longer listing.
Fields are separated by tabs.
.TP
.B \-\-columns
Aligned listing for the console, with a heading row.
Implies
.BR \-v .
Bytes and parameter counts are scaled.
Shard and detail columns appear only when a member has them.
Applies to list or info.
.TP
.B \-\-fold
Merge a consecutive numeric name segment when the tensors match.
Implies
.BR \-\-columns .
.I model.layers.[3\-5]
is one copy of each leaf, not the sum, and the offset is
.IR \- .
A gap, or a second number in the name, stays on its own line.
Applies to list or info.
.B tensdiff \-\-fold
folds a diff the same way.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-directory " \fIdir\fR"
Directory for extracted files.
The default is the current directory.
Applies to extract.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
Write the new archive here instead of replacing
.BR \-f .
Does not apply to list or info.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " name"
Container to read or write.
This build's names are printed when the name is unknown.
Which formats are compiled in is
.IR local/supported-formats.txt .
.I raw
is rawtensor/1, a
.I .rawtensor.json
manifest plus a
.IR .bin .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable listing or info on stdout.
.B \-\-columns
and
.B \-\-fold
do not apply to
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BI \-\-dtype " name"
Dtype for a headerless input file.
A safetensors name or a canonical id.
.TP
.BI \-\-shape " list"
Shape for a headerless input, for example
.I 2,2
or
.IR [2,2] .
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata " key=value"
Set a text metadata entry on create or update.
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata\-file " file"
JSON object of metadata.
GGUF values are typed.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-header\-size " size"
Safetensors header cap.
The default is 100M.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing file on create or extract.
.TP
.BI \-\-force\-single\-file " path"
Read this
.I .safetensors
file even when
.I config.json
is in the same directory.
It applies only to the path written immediately after it.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan and do not write.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the short help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH MEMBERS
A bare name selects a member for list, extract, or delete.
.PP
.I key=path
adds or replaces from a file.
A bare
.I .npy
uses its file stem as the key.
.PP
.I key=archive:member
copies one member out of another container.
.PP
A bare
.I .npz
on create, append, or update imports every array in the archive.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation finished.
.TP
.B 1
An error.
The message is written to stderr and starts with
.BR "tenspile: " .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B tenspile \-tvf model.safetensors
.B tenspile \-t \-\-columns \-\-fold \-f model.safetensors
.B tenspile \-i model.gguf
.B tenspile \-xf model.safetensors \-C out embed
.B tenspile \-cf out.safetensors embed=embed.npy \-\-metadata format=pt
.B tenspile \-uf model.safetensors norm=new_norm.npy
.B tenspile \-\-delete \-f model.safetensors optimizer.step
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tensdiff (1),
.BR tensconv (1),
.BR tensquant (1)
